-- title:
--   The subgroup reachable from the identity
-- statement:
--   For any group $G$ and subset $S$, take the elements reachable from the identity in the simple multiplication Cayley graph generated by $S$. Equip this set with its subgroup structure, using graph reachability for membership. The identity belongs by the empty path; the construction is valid without assuming $S$ generates the whole group. It packages Cayley graph connectivity as an algebraic subgroup for generation arguments.
